{
  "moduleId": "m00271",
  "title": {
    "segmentId": "m00271:title:auto-1",
    "text": "Biosynthesis of Steroids"
  },
  "documentClass": null,
  "metadata": {
    "uuid": "2672124b-3a1b-415e-941c-f755b2ceb9fa"
  },
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00001",
      "segmentId": "m00271:para:para-00001"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00001",
      "class": "scaled-down",
      "caption": {
        "segmentId": "m00271:caption:fig-00001-caption"
      },
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00271:alt:fig-00001-alt",
          "text": "Two farnesyl diphosphate molecules undergo dimerization to form squalene which cyclizes to lanosterol. This leads to the formation of steroids."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_27_07_001.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00002",
      "segmentId": "m00271:para:para-00002"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00003",
      "segmentId": "m00271:para:para-00003"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00002",
      "class": "scaled-down",
      "caption": {
        "segmentId": "m00271:caption:fig-00002-caption"
      },
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00271:alt:fig-00002-alt",
          "text": "Squalene undergoes expoxidation to form (3 S)-2,3-oxidosqualene via flavin adenine dinucleotide hydroperoxide, generated from flavin adenine dinucleotide dihydrogen and molecular oxygen."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_27_07_002.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "sect-00010",
      "class": null,
      "title": {
        "segmentId": "m00271:title:sect-00010-title",
        "text": "Steps 1, 2 of [[xref:fig-00004]]: Epoxide Opening and Initial Cyclizations"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00001",
          "class": null,
          "title": null,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00004",
              "segmentId": "m00271:para:para-00004"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00003",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00271:alt:fig-00003-alt",
                  "text": "Acid-promoted ring opening of (3 S)-2,3-oxidosqualene undergoes two cationic cyclizations to form a decaline ring with carbocation at C 8."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_27_07_003.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00002",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00271:title:sect-00002-title",
            "text": "Step 3 of [[xref:fig-00004]]: Third Cyclization"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00005",
              "segmentId": "m00271:para:para-00005"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00004",
              "class": "mechanism-figure scaled-down",
              "caption": {
                "segmentId": "m00271:caption:fig-00004-caption"
              },
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00271:alt:fig-00004-alt",
                  "text": "A four-step reaction mechanism in the formation of protosteryl cation from (3 S)-2,3-oxidosqualene."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_27_07_004.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00005",
              "class": "mechanism-figure scaled-down",
              "caption": {
                "segmentId": "m00271:caption:fig-00005-caption"
              },
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00271:alt:fig-00005-alt",
                  "text": "The remaining five steps in the formation of lanosterol where the protosteryl cation undergoes five rearragnments."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_27_07_005.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00006",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00271:alt:fig-00006-alt",
                  "text": "The intermediate generated at the second step of oxidation of (3 S)-2,3-oxidosqualene forms tricyclic secondary and tertiary carbocations."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_27_07_006.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00003",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00271:title:sect-00003-title",
            "text": "Step 4 of [[xref:fig-00004]]: Final Cyclization"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00006",
              "segmentId": "m00271:para:para-00006"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00007",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00271:alt:fig-00007-alt",
                  "text": "The intermediate generated at the third step undergoes cyclization to form protosteryl cation."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_27_07_007.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00004",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00271:title:sect-00004-title",
            "text": "Steps 5–9 of [[xref:fig-00004]]: Carbocation Rearrangements"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00007",
              "segmentId": "m00271:para:para-00007"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00008",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00271:alt:fig-00008-alt",
                  "text": "A base reacts with the protosteryl cation to form lanosterol. The reaction mechanism is denoted by multiple arrows."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_27_07_008.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00008",
              "segmentId": "m00271:para:para-00008"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00009",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00271:alt:fig-00009-alt",
                  "text": "Lanosterol forms cholesterol via a double bond rearrangement and a double bond reduction."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_27_07_009.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
